 inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }0<y<{x}^{2},\\\\\\,0<x<1\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"} :activity/title "Open and Closed Sets" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481577} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481741}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198787 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26758016-ed47-562a-9338-85c71ffbeaa9" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Derivatives" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049070 :topic/id #uuid "d79ee816-b7eb-5805-856a-502f9a6adaa4" :topic/math-academy-id 4386 :topic/title "Infinite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8f53bd8-9ef9-57f4-8a63-cec3891f5e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459699} {:answer/id #uuid "1ffae41e-b8f8-54f4-bbf2-3f0a2cc9c3a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8f53bd8-9ef9-57f4-8a63-cec3891f5e01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459699} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a2266ca-93a8-5492-80b5-97a981aaf710" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}A=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}({x}^{2})\\,:\\\\\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460716} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b29a5306-4144-5f79-908a-f8feff4ba33a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459701} {:answer/id #uuid "03e9eb1b-02d8-506f-82f1-512dd85f1977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03e9eb1b-02d8-506f-82f1-512dd85f1977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459702} :answer-field/id #uuid "0cfa2ff5-23d6-55fb-acac-2e57ae1265d5" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}B=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\,:\\\\\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460717} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad9d171-6dd3-541c-afb8-e1779bf6036a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459703} {:answer/id #uuid "d7e2da5c-32be-56a9-8008-4e08536eb809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7e2da5c-32be-56a9-8008-4e08536eb809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459704} :answer-field/id #uuid "a85a6640-66d8-5a27-8abe-3ec0ab8d48ff" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}C=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\sqrt{x})\\,:\\\\\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460718}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e02e6bd4-a148-57c6-a612-60228a140b9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-181599" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements. \n\n- The set $A$ is finite. Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & ={x}^{2} \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})=2x \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x)=2 \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2)=0 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(0)=0 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, for $n>3,$ we have ${f}^{(n)}(x)=0.$ Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\nA={{x}^{2},2x,2,0}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|A|=4,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $B$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {g}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nB={\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\\frac{1}{x},-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},-\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Similar to the previous case, listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =\\sqrt{x} \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}})=-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}} \\\\ {h}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}})=\\frac{3}{8\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nC={\\sqrt{x},\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}},-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}},\\frac{3}{8\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ and $C$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186231429 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cac41120-247d-5821-b7f6-b342dbcf8f18" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Solutions to Forced Harmonic Motion Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048966 :topic/id #uuid "cfd9de67-b6d3-5aac-81ab-498c732e22a6" :topic/math-academy-id 6720 :topic/title "Resonance in Vibrating Systems"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b10f3398-95fb-51ac-819d-349fa3583218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462315} {:answer/id #uuid "93d77f90-d255-502e-a3d2-a8904ab3576f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93d77f90-d255-502e-a3d2-a8904ab3576f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462316} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6a3385f-3cab-5129-83bb-f7a582ea68df" :answer-field/key "$y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)-\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462911} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15a268ac-7559-5f46-bf6c-3d1043ac53f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462317} {:answer/id #uuid "47e07c54-ee13-5022-a287-d6f6ab82ff3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15a268ac-7559-5f46-bf6c-3d1043ac53f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462317} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b82a872-8326-5513-8f4a-ccff55e33bb4" :answer-field/key "$y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)+3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462912} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa10a572-2a12-5313-a511-b89c8f024781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462319} {:answer/id #uuid "f79ee182-a849-5b22-a888-28a5c0d2851d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa10a572-2a12-5313-a511-b89c8f024781" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462319} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc60cb7-562c-5b04-bbc2-febf547f3bde" :answer-field/key "$y$ $=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ $+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$ $-3t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ $+t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "28a570c8-4263-5a25-a7a9-87fb602a6de5" :question/math-academy-id "q-343490" :question/problem "A particle is moving with forced harmonic motion without damping. The particle is acted on by an external periodic force\n$f(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$\nAssuming the system experiences resonance, which of the following could be used to represent the general solution for the position $y(t)?$\n\nNote that $A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $1.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =1.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡t).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =1$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(2D-Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-(2C+Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)]+t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 2D\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-2C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and $D=0.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=-\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)-\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+ϕ)-\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$\n\nOnly solution $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)-\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ matches the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+ϕ)-\\frac{3}{2}t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048966 :topic/id #uuid "cfd9de67-b6d3-5aac-81ab-498c732e22a6" :topic/math-academy-id 6720 :topic/title "Resonance in Vibrating Systems"} :activity/title "Resonance in Vibrating Systems" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481572} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481691}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853427ec-ff39-510f-b5b9-b9b3063c4fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422189} {:answer/id #uuid "26f5c7b4-02a7-523d-971a-7bb512830680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422190 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409287 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26f5c7b4-02a7-523d-971a-7bb512830680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422190 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409287 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "f073f5b0-a749-5824-acf4-fa526c4e38fd" :answer-field/key "$(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422375} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2303430c-0704-550c-b6ae-374bc966f21d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422191 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409287 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a09a9d-3bac-5120-8742-15c47fbf484c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2303430c-0704-550c-b6ae-374bc966f21d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422191 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409287 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "66f00add-7f80-5655-aba8-bf0b7b031d57" :answer-field/key "$8{y}^{′}-xy=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e36a2e5-c84a-5bb7-86bc-439a8b342c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422193 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409287 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} {:answer/id #uuid "707a477f-c377-547a-845c-170d00c19430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e36a2e5-c84a-5bb7-86bc-439a8b342c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422193 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409287 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "e13181d5-74b1-59ab-977c-f7a710603e44" :answer-field/key "$3{y}^{″}$ $=4y,$ $\\,y(-1)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(-1)$ $=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7775ce93-f97a-564e-ab19-6ca38ffa6f3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-118786" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y$ together with the initial condition $y(-1)=3.$\n\n- System $8{y}^{′}-xy=3$ is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\n- System $3{y}^{″}$ $=4y,$ $\\,y(-1)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(-1)$ $=1$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $3{y}^{″}=4y$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=1.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$ only." :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409287 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 42.294 :task-item/id #uuid "79a12f04-0672-43ad-ae4e-daa3cac99bb1" :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "26f5c7b4-02a7-523d-971a-7bb512830680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422190} {:answer/id #uuid "2303430c-0704-550c-b6ae-374bc966f21d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422191} {:answer/id #uuid "6e36a2e5-c84a-5bb7-86bc-439a8b342c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422193}] :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31ed816f-dcc9-55e7-a7ee-b8893ddc6b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422345 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576126 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} {:answer/id #uuid "7c033af8-4e67-5059-a3d7-2ee152e006ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31ed816f-dcc9-55e7-a7ee-b8893ddc6b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422345 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576126 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "25e14789-c319-5f0e-bc5c-74e15f504fc6" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}{y}^{''}-y$ $=2x,$ $\\,y(1)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{'}(1)$ $=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422453} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "891fce35-cd60-5014-954c-b452492c406b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422347 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576126 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} {:answer/id #uuid "c19a760c-5182-53bb-9e1c-45300e79eda9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "891fce35-cd60-5014-954c-b452492c406b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422347 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576126 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "88417ad9-d92d-5c8a-9985-1095d72e3b30" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{‴}-{e}^{x}{y}^{'}$ $=9y,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{'}(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{''}(0)$ $=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422454} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1015ba8-7c86-5225-bd73-031db89ebe78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422349} {:answer/id #uuid "7b79acea-a0fa-5455-a4fd-773c08b30342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422350 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576126 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b79acea-a0fa-5455-a4fd-773c08b30342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422350 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576126 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]} :answer-field/id #uuid "a349157e-eeba-5e25-b578-93131466b86c" :answer-field/key "$2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y},\\,y(0)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85607d47-df50-5e10-bf9d-699a7a42f32f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96987" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{'}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System ${x}^{2}{y}^{''}-y$ $=2x,$ $\\,y(1)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{'}(1)$ $=3$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{''}-y=2x$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(1)=1,\\,{y}^{'}(1)=3.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\n- System $x{y}^{‴}-{e}^{x}{y}^{'}$ $=9y,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{'}(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{''}(0)$ $=2$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *third*-order differential equation $x{y}^{‴}-{e}^{x}{y}^{'}=9y$ together with *three* initial conditions $y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{'}(0)=1,$ and ${y}^{''}(0)=2.$ This is a third-order initial value problem.\n\n- System $2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y},\\,y(0)=1$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y}$ together with the initial condition $y(0)=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $2{y}^{'}-\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{y},\\,y(0)=1$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"} :activity/title "Review: Introduction to Differential Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569395} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569397}] :task-item/_content [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576126 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234496} :task-item/elapsed-seconds 37.184 :task-item/id #uuid "a542f67b-6e61-4795-a70e-02f36878e6a3" :task-item/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186576127} :task-item/responses [{:answer/id #uuid "31ed816f-dcc9-55e7-a7ee-b8893ddc6b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422345} {:answer/id #uuid "891fce35-cd60-5014-954c-b452492c406b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422347} {:answer/id #uuid "7b79acea-a0fa-5455-a4fd-773c08b30342" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422350}] :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571} :task-item/working-ended-at #inst "2026-10-17T18:11:03.021Z"}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048614 :topic/id #uuid "aedeae90-38bd-5345-9896-abb52aad6dc6" :topic/math-academy-id 2002 :topic/title "Point Discontinuities"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58795638-a192-5cb2-add6-072256161aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461297} {:answer/id #uuid "f8618f49-d2bc-5685-9c55-7c8a9a585828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8618f49-d2bc-5685-9c55-7c8a9a585828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461298} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0bfa1fe-ca62-5b36-b004-861e91cb01da" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}g(x)$ $={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}g(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7b4c029-937e-5c36-8214-90b1d5fad103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461299} {:answer/id #uuid "a90f0d06-6d6c-5382-abcc-8217128de6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a90f0d06-6d6c-5382-abcc-8217128de6f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461300} :answer-field/id #uuid "983a7b3f-b174-5765-9406-806dfae93ca7" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462403} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58c82481-105a-5321-9ff8-563c4fbcd6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461301} {:answer/id #uuid "a016123d-7112-5014-9f4b-ef79f653d073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58c82481-105a-5321-9ff8-563c4fbcd6a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461301} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3cf173a-51b1-50ec-858a-e45fc5b1d0e6" :answer-field/key "$g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bdde4d8-daa6-55ef-bcc6-21f99b29d77c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104575" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-34, & x<-3 \\\\ -25, & x=-3 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2, & x>-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $g(-3)=-25$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{-}}({x}^{2}-34)=(-3)^{2}-34=-25, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{+}}({x}^{3}+2)=(-3)^{3}+2=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude that statement ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}g(x)$ $={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}g(x)$ is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=-25.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The value of the limit is ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=-25,$ and the value of the function is $g(-3)=-25.$ So, statement ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)$ is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, the function is continuous at $x=-3,$ and statement “$g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=-3$” is false.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}g(x)$ $={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)$ are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d474031-aec8-57ab-a3e0-55a89435cf1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461437} {:answer/id #uuid "f7daefe6-fc8a-5e47-94be-0a48f56ddf85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7daefe6-fc8a-5e47-94be-0a48f56ddf85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461438} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0382769-e42c-58d2-b541-6e4e6dcc2ec8" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0<y\\le {x}^{3}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2f5aa7e-d32d-5d0c-bdfe-e74efc085aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461439} {:answer/id #uuid "87addec4-73f4-5600-859d-f2a3ae0b54df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2f5aa7e-d32d-5d0c-bdfe-e74efc085aec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461439} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a01675-4425-5843-ba6e-097451cce680" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}-y<0}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c37fb727-928e-5d8e-8476-07eb63595218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461441} {:answer/id #uuid "73e840dd-1ac0-5de2-bcb8-fb0e704477a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73e840dd-1ac0-5de2-bcb8-fb0e704477a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461442} :answer-field/id #uuid "4899626b-7729-58f3-a88d-468c0c77f306" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\\\\\,-{x}^{4}<y<{x}^{4}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9f390fe-da40-537a-ae87-c6dfb93153a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105423" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(1,1).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some boundary points, for example, the point $(1,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (the corresponding inequality is strict).\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,16).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,-1\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0<y\\le {x}^{3}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\\\\\,-{x}^{4}<y<{x}^{4}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241054 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ab35358-6a6e-53c9-a359-2eeb55169a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461443} {:answer/id #uuid "01e83318-19e7-5daf-8d94-d46c64997a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01e83318-19e7-5daf-8d94-d46c64997a7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461444} :answer-field/id #uuid "40249fef-4857-5239-88aa-35f1ab209488" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,2\\le x\\le 6,\\\\\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462475} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9e5add6-21ff-5127-afaf-df7c753a3119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461445} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5aa1e0-c811-5a3c-9e71-6de7dd2c4260" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9e5add6-21ff-5127-afaf-df7c753a3119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461445} :answer-field/id #uuid "058d3ef2-cefd-5d09-853d-5e64f8233ce5" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0<{x}^{2}<9,\\\\\\,1<{y}^{2}<16\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462476} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "491a04b5-b27e-564f-9f59-d114e4ce4441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461447} {:answer/id #uuid "d8df605e-3807-5915-bab0-6e1df41880af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "491a04b5-b27e-564f-9f59-d114e4ce4441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461447} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3473981-d1e7-5830-8430-e252ede45aab" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2},\\\\\\,-2\\le x\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2d4a59fe-0871-5826-aa72-1fb9c0a2dad6" :question/math-academy-id "q-105431" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(2,\\sqrt{3}).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(2,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,2\\le x\\le 6,\\\\\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"} :activity/title "Open and Closed Sets" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409697} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409714}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241058 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8da227c0-43c3-53af-b829-2b5e45fe613e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461449} {:answer/id #uuid "847d8a11-3b7f-5099-8561-09e695d74f2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8da227c0-43c3-53af-b829-2b5e45fe613e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461449} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d3162c5-3925-574f-b0da-e3491f823f6e" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }x+y<4,\\\\\\,-1<x<4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462478} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8880c6df-b262-5a08-9751-ccec61a1adfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461451} {:answer/id #uuid "c9119b74-7810-557e-b9ca-00afabe65407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9119b74-7810-557e-b9ca-00afabe65407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461452} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae4c6abe-cabb-5a92-afb6-9e51398743ff" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }0\\le x<4,\\\\\\,2<y\\le 4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462479} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a95f0ca7-e174-5653-afa2-634c73938177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461453} {:answer/id #uuid "37738e30-2b54-557d-bee1-1f04ec248585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37738e30-2b54-557d-bee1-1f04ec248585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461454} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c4767ef-a476-5c1f-b66a-dae088dd8bb1" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }-1\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,2<y<4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462480}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9d461bff-0ae1-55fc-a03d-01dfa63c39ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-105437" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any point of its boundary (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(3,2).$\n\n- The third set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(-1,3).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }0\\le x<4,\\\\\\,2<y\\le 4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }-1\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,2<y<4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243955 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a914512e-7672-5333-8b5c-b71fba7518f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447790} {:answer/id #uuid "dd0cd5bb-20fe-5d02-8a73-e9965b60629a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a914512e-7672-5333-8b5c-b71fba7518f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447790} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd22bb13-41fa-5ad4-87ca-4ebdbb8f9c9c" :answer-field/key "For any $f(x)\\in N,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448935} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8475cd02-dfa7-555e-8fe6-af9c1b3dfd1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447792} {:answer/id #uuid "0acd572a-df4e-5da4-ab5c-fa2488c8f02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0acd572a-df4e-5da4-ab5c-fa2488c8f02f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447793} :answer-field/id #uuid "38a03ef7-085c-5065-a4eb-5d8739f0a73b" :answer-field/key "For any $f(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448936} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bfc222dc-bcd7-58fe-b427-0f883e3ace51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447794} {:answer/id #uuid "2c767313-26ce-5c29-9d65-ec7d48a44dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447795}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c767313-26ce-5c29-9d65-ec7d48a44dd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447795} :answer-field/id #uuid "0652d0f5-63c7-5c09-b3ab-489157c2a0ca" :answer-field/key "For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))$ $=\\alpha f(x)$ $+\\alpha g(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448937}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d83ac51c-0c75-5956-b55e-b6c1972a1661" :question/math-academy-id "q-106809" :question/problem "Let $N$ be the set of all functions of the form $f(x)=a|x|,$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “For any $f(x)\\in N,$ we have $(-1)\\cdot f(x)=f(x).$” is false. As a counterexample, consider $f(x)=|x|\\in N.$ Then,\n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot f(x)=(-1)\\cdot |x|=-|x|\\ne |x|.\n$$\n\nHence, $(-1)\\cdot f(x)\\ne f(x).$\n\n- Statement “For any $f(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any function $f(x)\\in N$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))$ $=\\alpha f(x)$ $+\\alpha g(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any functions $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and any fixed $x\\in R,$ the results of $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $f(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$”; “For any $f(x),g(x)\\in N$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))$ $=\\alpha f(x)$ $+\\alpha g(x).$” only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/title "Quiz 11" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547297} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548148}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243956 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058509a8-3ac9-575c-988e-870fd00ccd59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447796} {:answer/id #uuid "a85b2c8a-71ea-5f1a-a8ac-2e7466a283f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "058509a8-3ac9-575c-988e-870fd00ccd59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447796} :answer-field/id #uuid "4114966c-2da1-5b38-afb3-c02c26536f47" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{x}\\in J$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448938} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6be2e356-52d5-5de3-9011-6050919c0a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447798} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a2f597-17fa-529c-ab15-d944ea368bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3a2f597-17fa-529c-ab15-d944ea368bb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447799} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1628d5f-e29e-5fe9-9187-304c2dd12982" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x)\\in J,$ we have $1\\cdot p(x)\\in J$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448939} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c6cdaa-bc0a-5ab7-bbec-8ba025d53be2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447800} {:answer/id #uuid "f02b3fc3-9656-50ca-b527-29ec38bebafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f02b3fc3-9656-50ca-b527-29ec38bebafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447801} :answer-field/id #uuid "a452f612-5cea-59f2-93e3-d66f0c20ebce" :answer-field/key "For any $p(x),q(x)\\in J$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))$ $=\\alpha p(x)$ $-\\alpha q(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448940}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "253cf041-a7dc-53ad-a439-778e84d95095" :question/math-academy-id "q-106810" :question/problem "Let $J$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is at most $2.$  Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\frac{1}{x}\\in J$ is false. The set $J$ contains only polynomials whose degree is at most $2.$ However, $\\frac{1}{x}$ is *not* a polynomial. So, $\\frac{1}{x}\\notin J.$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x)\\in J,$ we have $1\\cdot p(x)\\in J$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x)\\in J$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the result of $p(x)$ is just a real number. Thus,\n\n$$\n1\\cdot p(x)=p(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $p(x),q(x)\\in J$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))$ $=\\alpha p(x)$ $-\\alpha q(x)$” is true. Indeed, for any $p(x),q(x)\\in J,$ and for any fixed $x\\in R,$ the results of $p(x)$ and $q(x)$ are just real numbers. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))=\\alpha p(x)-\\alpha q(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “For any $p(x)\\in J,$ we have $1\\cdot p(x)\\in J$”; “For any $p(x),q(x)\\in J$ and $\\alpha \\in R,$ we have $\\alpha (p(x)-q(x))$ $=\\alpha p(x)$ $-\\alpha q(x)$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1094661c-8c7c-5f85-b731-4dadb0aec310" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Using Set Notation Are Subspaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048337 :topic/id #uuid "96874e3b-8b97-5c33-995d-d34a9d3daf21" :topic/math-academy-id 4077 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea812525-5990-52cf-b86e-78f1b4de8995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461647} {:answer/id #uuid "8f213eb6-2142-5889-90e4-c372925d0dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea812525-5990-52cf-b86e-78f1b4de8995" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461647} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9799888-3637-5f54-acd6-ed3396e155dd" :answer-field/key "$A={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:xyz=1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3af6b52c-a109-53f6-aa27-67a8c43708cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461649} {:answer/id #uuid "ff863854-8a24-5221-be5f-d347d25b3c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff863854-8a24-5221-be5f-d347d25b3c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461650} :answer-field/id #uuid "87c50586-e18a-5fca-a9fa-4b003d93b2c7" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}B=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\\\x+y-z=0\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462578} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f70460d9-df3a-58dd-95a2-bafff6dc83d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461651} {:answer/id #uuid "61868caa-f76b-5288-8ca4-5d353e006f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f70460d9-df3a-58dd-95a2-bafff6dc83d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461651} :answer-field/id #uuid "18092fb5-74d5-5ff7-870d-5e5eab99935e" :answer-field/key "$C={⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:y=-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462579}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3d55fbe8-7170-5840-8a9a-b1f2a55c58fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-110611" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $xyz=1$ since $0\\cdot 0\\cdot 0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x+y-z=0$ since $0+0-0=0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the condition $y=-1$ since $0\\ne -1.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}B=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\\\x+y-z=0\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247159 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1094661c-8c7c-5f85-b731-4dadb0aec310" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Using Set Notation Are Subspaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048337 :topic/id #uuid "96874e3b-8b97-5c33-995d-d34a9d3daf21" :topic/math-academy-id 4077 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ba35c72-4811-55d0-b2b1-fb8116a2cc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461653} {:answer/id #uuid "8d2a422a-84a1-5671-bc55-3b45224e58cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ba35c72-4811-55d0-b2b1-fb8116a2cc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461653} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0888cfa-5fff-5bcc-9c6f-d3cf0a398b99" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}A=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\\\x-4y=1\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462580} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2974aa62-0b1f-5343-a4a5-c39a1584c078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461655} {:answer/id #uuid "78c8ebf0-1d54-5046-ae1c-3426546d3565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78c8ebf0-1d54-5046-ae1c-3426546d3565" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461656} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad91d256-6b2d-51b9-8149-c46bca013503" :answer-field/key "$B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x=-2y\\}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5784de9d-74b4-5c34-9c61-2b2f1a7172ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461657} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa10535-80e6-5c1d-a5e9-5bed7b7ca613" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5784de9d-74b4-5c34-9c61-2b2f1a7172ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461657} :answer-field/id #uuid "822bc400-c192-58d1-80df-f14e9a428a6a" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}C=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:\\\\{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "49bd226a-4547-5889-a62c-e6c2912a1520" :question/math-academy-id "q-110760" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each subset.\n\n- The set $A$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. For instance, $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $x-4y=1$ since $0-4\\cdot 0=0\\ne 1.$\n\n- The set $B$ is a subspace. It represents a plane, and a plane is a subspace if and only if it passes through the origin. Here, the components of the zero vector $0=⟨0,0,0⟩$ satisfy the equation $x=-2y$ since $0=-2\\cdot 0.$ So $0$ lies in $B.$\n\n- The set $C$ is not a subspace. No point in ${R}^{3}$ satisfies the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}<0.$ Hence, $C=∅.$ The empty set is not a subspace since it does not contain the zero vector.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $B=\\{⟨x,y,z⟩\\in {R}^{3}:x=-2y\\}$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048337 :topic/id #uuid "96874e3b-8b97-5c33-995d-d34a9d3daf21" :topic/math-academy-id 4077 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation"} :activity/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434588} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434599}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fc37352-81e0-514c-bedf-fa91579d6398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422195} {:answer/id #uuid "00fbec5e-2569-5e70-887a-76fd721447ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "00fbec5e-2569-5e70-887a-76fd721447ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422196} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d2c7ba3-872a-5747-84b2-d758a496b0c6" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}-x=-7y,\\,y(2)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d471821-5101-5272-a1e9-64c5df191a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422197} {:answer/id #uuid "e79714fa-47cd-53d1-87a1-cb84a5b63e67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6d471821-5101-5272-a1e9-64c5df191a7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422197} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6f72266-3ebb-5e6f-a355-a91fc75722dc" :answer-field/key "${x}^{4}{y}^{‴}+3y$ $={2}^{y},$ $\\,y(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(0)$ $=-1,$ $\\,{y}^{″}(0)$ $=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d77c166-99a6-5b75-9890-9bbf922be8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422199} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d66aee-5929-509b-ad21-8bd403ae74fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d77c166-99a6-5b75-9890-9bbf922be8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422199} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b0ca13e-0a9c-5b4c-8a39-481f747b601a" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{″}-6y$ $=14,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=-3,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(0)$ $=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4247b2af-dd08-543e-82b1-e9616731f453" :question/math-academy-id "q-118787" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System ${y}^{′}-x=-7y,\\,y(2)=3$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation ${y}^{′}-x=-7y$ together with the initial condition $y(2)=3.$\n\n- System ${x}^{4}{y}^{‴}+3y$ $={2}^{y},$ $\\,y(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(0)$ $=-1,$ $\\,{y}^{″}(0)$ $=0$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *third*-order differential equation ${x}^{4}{y}^{‴}+3y={2}^{y}$ together with *three* initial conditions $y(0)=1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-1,$ and ${y}^{″}(0)=0.$ This is a third-order initial value problem.\n\n- System $x{y}^{″}-6y$ $=14,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=-3,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(0)$ $=3$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $x{y}^{″}-6y=14$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(0)=-3,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=3.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}-x=-7y,\\,y(2)=3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "289bb35b-99fe-5106-99b0-f71c04163a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422201} {:answer/id #uuid "2302fbb6-0adc-5661-bbf7-af76484dacc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "289bb35b-99fe-5106-99b0-f71c04163a88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422201} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e48c6aa-29b3-5af2-98e8-cf9155d9f86e" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}{y}^{‴}+9{x}^{3}{y}^{′}$ $=-7y,$ $\\,y(0)$ $={y}^{′}(0)$ $={y}^{″}(0)$ $=-4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422381} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "beef713f-b9cc-55dc-8f1d-6cf37ec09f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422203} {:answer/id #uuid "e499fae0-7b48-5f3b-93bb-81ab64c9da66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e499fae0-7b48-5f3b-93bb-81ab64c9da66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422204} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbae87b9-4781-5997-879b-2dc1d3b6b122" :answer-field/key "$x{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=6,\\,y(0)=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aac407af-d819-550f-805d-c2f156435fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422205} {:answer/id #uuid "983242a4-a136-5392-8243-ada487eed7f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aac407af-d819-550f-805d-c2f156435fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422205} :answer-field/id #uuid "259806e0-5727-5f05-a402-006bfaa14dbc" :answer-field/key "$6{y}^{″}+xy={e}^{x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422383}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "941e9c2c-1b18-5669-bb2b-964e53cd46ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-118788" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System ${x}^{2}{y}^{‴}+9{x}^{3}{y}^{′}$ $=-7y,$ $\\,y(0)$ $={y}^{′}(0)$ $={y}^{″}(0)$ $=-4$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *third*-order differential equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{‴}+9{x}^{3}{y}^{′}=-7y$ together with *three* initial conditions $y(0)={y}^{′}(0)={y}^{″}(0)=-4.$ This is a third-order initial value problem.\n\n- System $x{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=6,\\,y(0)=2$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $x{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=6$ together with the initial condition $y(0)=2.$\n\n- System $6{y}^{″}+xy={e}^{x}$ is not a first-order initial value problem. We have here a second-order ordinary differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=6,\\,y(0)=2$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253515 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e5caf84-b369-53c1-92d8-3daf6511f002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422213} {:answer/id #uuid "d814dbc8-353f-574a-8589-9891a880a534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e5caf84-b369-53c1-92d8-3daf6511f002" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422213} :answer-field/id #uuid "66d4f45e-d07b-5e2f-a6dc-8a5dc04ecd85" :answer-field/key "${y}^{‴}+{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+y$ $=0,$ $\\,y(1)$ $={y}^{′}(1)$ $={y}^{″}(1)$ $=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422387} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fccfea10-d196-5af8-881d-6efaf713593e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422215} {:answer/id #uuid "26116a3c-17a4-5e07-abc8-396b55612f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26116a3c-17a4-5e07-abc8-396b55612f60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422216} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f1b9058-f874-55f5-b4b3-7338f7856cb8" :answer-field/key "${y}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y={3}^{x},\\,y(1)=6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10764352-ef44-5719-87cb-3b2d8938735f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422217} {:answer/id #uuid "e37e4e1a-2748-569f-9af1-4faf43505566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e37e4e1a-2748-569f-9af1-4faf43505566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422218} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcab1241-b9e2-53d5-94b4-15742cef1c28" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{x}{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=6,\\,y(4)=-3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7204e641-7358-50b0-b9c2-d492a160bc98" :question/math-academy-id "q-118791" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System ${y}^{‴}+{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+y$ $=0,$ $\\,y(1)$ $={y}^{′}(1)$ $={y}^{″}(1)$ $=2$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *third*-order differential equation ${y}^{‴}+{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+y=0$ together with *three* initial conditions $y(1)={y}^{′}(1)={y}^{″}(1)=2.$ This is a third-order initial value problem.\n\n- System ${y}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y={3}^{x},\\,y(1)=6$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation ${y}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y={3}^{x}$ together with the initial condition $y(1)=6.$\n\n- System $\\sqrt{x}{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=6,\\,y(4)=-3$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $\\sqrt{x}{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=6$ together with the initial condition $y(4)=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${y}^{′}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+y={3}^{x},\\,y(1)=6$; $\\sqrt{x}{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=6,\\,y(4)=-3$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049592 :topic/id #uuid "02ecb448-e544-51fa-b80e-63ee84a4cef1" :topic/math-academy-id 3215 :topic/title "Introduction to Differential Equations"} :activity/title "Review: Introduction to Differential Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569395} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569400}]} 