,{z}^{5}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c750739b-5adf-51bf-8122-bbc865b012bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437628} {:answer/id #uuid "16c760f1-2a00-532d-8ab5-17d51057a421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c750739b-5adf-51bf-8122-bbc865b012bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437628} :answer-field/id #uuid "23d9d23a-b11c-50ab-a519-b5ea13ec3cca" :answer-field/key "$C(t)=⟨2-{t}^{2},{e}^{t-1}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "212db81f-3e39-5c00-88aa-953a8a56ffb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-122653" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $A(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,|\\,x+y>0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $B(x,y,z)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $C(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$  It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $A(x,y)$ $=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y),\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256694 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b794e8c-8662-57a3-9430-d2ee2d5efdaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437648} {:answer/id #uuid "4de84e82-6689-5660-adc6-f0c83536a456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437649}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4de84e82-6689-5660-adc6-f0c83536a456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437649} :answer-field/id #uuid "616c4d45-069a-5832-84ae-5f981fb6e66f" :answer-field/key "$T(x,y,z)$ $=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,i$ $-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\,j$ $+{z}^{2}\\,k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438853} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51aecfc3-403e-5cba-b3b7-254b2d3ff5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437650} {:answer/id #uuid "1bb91534-359e-56df-b8a5-f99a590388aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51aecfc3-403e-5cba-b3b7-254b2d3ff5c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437650} :answer-field/id #uuid "f56d77cf-af96-5cc5-bb85-082f7d066b90" :answer-f