ulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16b71f57-df8c-5727-afc2-cdadae9185c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143334" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.6$ | $0.15$ | $0.75$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.7$ | $0.3$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=0,Y=3)$ $=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=3)=f(0,3)=0.15.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(3)=0.25\\cdot 0.3=0.075.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=3)\\ne P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=3),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050835 :topic/id #uuid "6a5936fb-0bab-5b84-a342-e13ec8019ebc" :topic/math-academy-id 3048 :topic/title "Independence of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd7e9f64-cbbd-5bbd-8464-3f61b6f11586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464288} {:answer/id #uuid "b46bc96b-ac7e-5f3f-a9a5-4cdfc8aba11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b46bc96b-ac7e-5f3f-a9a5-4cdfc8aba11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464289} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca347041-dadc-56e2-bbf1-f6ebc4c70e09" :answer-field/key "$P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e699ac2-764b-512c-8f0d-5172d00686da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464290} {:answer/id #uuid "006bf10f-88fe-5637-949f-4aa29407bc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e699ac2-764b-512c-8f0d-5172d00686da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464290} :answer-field/id #uuid "83f7c971-351f-53ff-be7e-c7304f5c86bf" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17db8ae0-64d6-5514-9124-5fa3d5e8dba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464292} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a98f0c-64a9-57fe-b332-0fefcb246690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17db8ae0-64d6-5514-9124-5fa3d5e8dba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464292} :answer-field/id #uuid "da33b576-bcf0-5c09-83dd-58d6caaeb72b" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "743eb09d-bf29-57ce-b05b-46da6dccd3f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143338" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.16$ | $0.01$ | $0.03$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.64$ | $0.09$ | $0.07$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.16$ | $0.01$ | $0.03$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.64$ | $0.09$ | $0.07$ | $0.8$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.8$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=3,Y=2)=f(3,2)=0.64.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.8\\cdot 0.8=0.64.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,2) & =0.16=0.2\\cdot 0.8={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓ \\\\ f(1,4) & =0.01\\ne 0.2\\cdot 0.1={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(4) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=3,Y=2)$ $=P(X=3)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275118 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050835 :topic/id #uuid "6a5936fb-0bab-5b84-a342-e13ec8019ebc" :topic/math-academy-id 3048 :topic/title "Independence of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2775cce0-304f-5113-963a-e28a11e24992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464294} {:answer/id #uuid "128d1ceb-39cf-5da3-8419-5a7d8a02044d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2775cce0-304f-5113-963a-e28a11e24992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464294} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d189a29-6c25-5569-854b-c13fc0526360" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465081} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad3a30bf-90ea-5614-8226-e124a25c10b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464296} {:answer/id #uuid "b3343df9-8a4a-5259-9ba0-3cd40ddbf9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad3a30bf-90ea-5614-8226-e124a25c10b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464296} :answer-field/id #uuid "af0ced41-0208-507d-b83f-0b656205df0e" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465082} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb8af9ea-b637-5ed4-b6ba-f9ad08c1f112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464298} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0da6fb-3bb6-55a5-a319-72bfe95326c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb8af9ea-b637-5ed4-b6ba-f9ad08c1f112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464298} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee63d585-1abb-575b-b286-f0fc73957802" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465083}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d571385e-cc3b-5950-8471-24ba60f93b53" :question/math-academy-id "q-143435" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.6$ | $0.7$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.25$ | $0.05$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.35$ | $0.65$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statements $P(X=1,Y=1)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)$ and “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” are false. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=1)=f(1,1)=0.05.$ However, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1)=0.3\\cdot 0.65=0.195.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nP(X=1,Y=1)\\ne P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=1),\n$$\n\nand $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of those listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278386 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c05d4f9-eb1b-59a1-ae0b-5d6869bad7c5" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type I Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175 :topic/id #uuid "85bac388-4397-5418-87a6-a1048f67cdda" :topic/math-academy-id 2130 :topic/title "Type I, II, and III Regions in Three-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dc900d5-6adb-5291-bb29-945c24e8a52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465375} {:answer/id #uuid "c5db8b48-0145-59b3-853e-2dc9a73f5319" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dc900d5-6adb-5291-bb29-945c24e8a52d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465375} :answer-field/id #uuid "6ba930a6-1b15-54d9-9b76-147214cfd918" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466531} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86f9f9d7-6a29-54a0-b78d-ab1ada5cb3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465377} {:answer/id #uuid "66070404-2e4d-59d0-81b6-d80fbc47cbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66070404-2e4d-59d0-81b6-d80fbc47cbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465378} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e459526-4e2e-5b5d-9c5a-53a2552e46e3" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,y)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=3-x+y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43c5d968-0c47-5b5c-af0a-2a7a009a838c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465379} {:answer/id #uuid "bf8627ef-3c0a-5dbb-bc99-ce2b4f5f165f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43c5d968-0c47-5b5c-af0a-2a7a009a838c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465379} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b4d526b-c9a0-5573-a72d-651b90ac9856" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,y)=1$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466533}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0b05250a-2126-54a5-8110-d92f7f2aa122" :question/math-academy-id "q-161117" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7bb6d2b9f9e09de44e078657ce3517bfd78261d3206743b7882abf0112f38a93.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=1$, $y=0$, $y=1$, $z=0,$ and $z=3-x+y.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,y)\\le z\\le {f}_{2}(x,y)}\n$$\n\nas a type I region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is false. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xy$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(x,y)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=3-x+y$” is true, while statement “${f}_{1}(x,y)=1$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=4$” is false. Indeed, we have\n\n- the *bottom* surface $z={f}_{1}(x,y)=0$, and\n\n- the *top* surface $z={f}_{2}(x,y)=3-x+y.$\n\n![](images/65/65e179e16b66009b9168c4380032b01c3a79b3c4a2afc3b8e5084defb77b85fc.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${f}_{1}(x,y)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=3-x+y$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278389 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c05d4f9-eb1b-59a1-ae0b-5d6869bad7c5" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type I Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175 :topic/id #uuid "85bac388-4397-5418-87a6-a1048f67cdda" :topic/math-academy-id 2130 :topic/title "Type I, II, and III Regions in Three-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cabb0a8d-aff4-57ab-96f0-f8d0915a925d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465381} {:answer/id #uuid "6578be7a-a203-5728-8f45-7417f3a0a68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6578be7a-a203-5728-8f45-7417f3a0a68c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465382} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7df53d5-584d-50cd-959b-c1935fb43d75" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466534} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76e10513-2430-594e-8305-5bb7ccc10a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465383} {:answer/id #uuid "5beefa76-4a9e-5425-8ae8-78a4b372ea51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76e10513-2430-594e-8305-5bb7ccc10a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465383} :answer-field/id #uuid "697d5114-f05b-5010-aa74-40202b0c59b3" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,y)=2$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=\\frac{15-4x}{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466535} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "79f1e02b-e929-5dcd-8dd3-1c7a56b7b8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465385} {:answer/id #uuid "61410729-3c43-570c-9bd4-40124d7efd17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465386}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79f1e02b-e929-5dcd-8dd3-1c7a56b7b8b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465385} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b954c2f-713e-5e8c-9abc-b9a072f0f21c" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,y)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "99aeb9ca-3424-5f18-af86-89763375eaeb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161125" :question/problem "![](images/e5/e5369264a9ab9328449bafd6fd3dcda1a70b7d90cbaf4f9815211e0cc3873fc0.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=3$, $y=0$, $y=2$, $z=0,$ and $4x+5z=15.$ Given its representation\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,y)\\le z\\le {f}_{2}(x,y)}\n$$\n\nas a type I region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xy$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(x,y)=2$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=\\frac{15-4x}{5}$” and statement “${f}_{1}(x,y)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=3$” are false. We have\n\n- the *bottom* surface $z={f}_{1}(x,y)=0$, and\n\n- the *top* surface $z={f}_{2}(x,y)=\\frac{15-4x}{5}.$\n\n![](images/ed/edea8af334c3362f583fcb86709150690eeec79a54185b67d242bfa14a8e4c75.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278403 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133818 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c05d4f9-eb1b-59a1-ae0b-5d6869bad7c5" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type I Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175 :topic/id #uuid "85bac388-4397-5418-87a6-a1048f67cdda" :topic/math-academy-id 2130 :topic/title "Type I, II, and III Regions in Three-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3dcc3ead-a5eb-59d5-b395-84368e02a2fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449904} {:answer/id #uuid "552b29d1-81b4-522d-a1e5-9344bd4cad3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "552b29d1-81b4-522d-a1e5-9344bd4cad3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449905} :answer-field/id #uuid "91461d3a-7bce-5e80-91c1-dce4ac1cc87d" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\,:\\\\\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a02cc7a9-2caf-5794-bb5c-7df397d6341f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449906} {:answer/id #uuid "69bf2c68-8883-5ae2-9be1-422c63c83c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a02cc7a9-2caf-5794-bb5c-7df397d6341f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449906} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c9d4940-8b58-5e01-be4b-3c772cf8c4ce" :answer-field/key "$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17d163fe-da7f-55c1-99a3-81e1b07d0123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449908} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b0d5a4-2df0-5a30-9edb-eaa989bafb4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449909}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17d163fe-da7f-55c1-99a3-81e1b07d0123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449908} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3ab31af-0692-56bd-b3dc-792901c29841" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=-2x-2y+6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e71e8fdb-04f6-527e-89b1-2171dc56e3a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161160" :question/problem "The region $R$ is bounded between the elliptic paraboloid $z=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ and the plane $z=-2x-2y+6.$ Given its representation\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,y)\\le z\\le {f}_{2}(x,y)}\n$$\n\nas a type I region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type I region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/05/05f940e247c6cd5d862d81fc3a34658353bef5513dfe862bbc67a120c0345838.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\,:\\\\\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true, while statement $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 2}$ is false. \n\nFirst, we find the projection of the intersection between the elliptic paraboloid $z=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ and the plane $z=-2x-2y+6$ onto $xy$-plane. \n\nNotice that the equation of the plane is already solved for $z.$ Substituting this expression for $z$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x-2y+6 & =8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}-2y & =2 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x+1)+({y}^{2}-2y+1) & =4 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo, the projection of the intersection is the circle $(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=4$ centered at $(1,1)$ in the $xy$-plane. Hence, the domain $D$ is given by the following disc:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 4}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ and ${f}_{2}(x,y)=-2x-2y+6$” is false. We have that $z$ is \n\n- bounded *below* by ${f}_{1}(x,y)=-2x-2y+6,$ and\n\n- bounded *above* by ${f}_{2}(x,y)=8-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\,:\\\\\\,(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}\\le 4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcc1bf5-5eea-5615-8b16-b8ced5de7984" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type II Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175 :topic/id #uuid "85bac388-4397-5418-87a6-a1048f67cdda" :topic/math-academy-id 2130 :topic/title "Type I, II, and III Regions in Three-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a5de68-5950-514f-9ba1-08fa9d4299ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465387} {:answer/id #uuid "99ded4e4-29f1-558a-9986-b3ec79c00a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99ded4e4-29f1-558a-9986-b3ec79c00a35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465388} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcb986ee-74d8-55e7-ace6-4c46cc82d2fa" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466537} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "805d79bd-85e2-5be6-930c-9af401f32ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465389} {:answer/id #uuid "9fc276e3-6d65-585e-9956-fe2637e49b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "805d79bd-85e2-5be6-930c-9af401f32ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465389} :answer-field/id #uuid "845a991c-16c1-5dca-bbbc-d4f135e22f63" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=2-y-z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466538} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e54cac66-bf9d-526e-b2f2-c9397de7dc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465391} {:answer/id #uuid "328852b4-a1a4-578a-9f26-a0109eec8aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e54cac66-bf9d-526e-b2f2-c9397de7dc54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465391} :answer-field/id #uuid "e14d9582-0fba-5cac-a562-27db433f61d6" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=2+y-z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "83e332b2-7a45-565f-946e-09fe8f179dcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161247" :question/problem "![](images/60/60f622b161dbfb4da1d18e85d3eb3ab4e02c2af418f9845e05a3bf9704a28006.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $y=0$, $y=3$, $z=0$, $z=2$, $x=0,$ and $x=2+y-z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e4/e4c9cbbad2f13e9cc125ddbb89125ed2d734eee3f80737125961f4af1846a972.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $yz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statements “${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=2-y-z$” and “${f}_{1}(y,z)=2+y-z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=5$” are false. We have\n\n- the *back* surface $x={f}_{1}(y,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *front* surface $x={f}_{2}(y,z)=2+y-z.$\n\n![](images/c2/c2af4029bd979d250ed15f351ef7f14d3ae688806db4ffec199a24b3591dadac.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278445 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dea8612-414c-5394-869d-1e404b048156" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type III Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175 :topic/id #uuid "85bac388-4397-5418-87a6-a1048f67cdda" :topic/math-academy-id 2130 :topic/title "Type I, II, and III Regions in Three-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b46cd556-9148-553e-a9ee-002da12838f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465393} {:answer/id #uuid "c81a3b20-2fa7-53cf-ba24-e30a9d7def19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c81a3b20-2fa7-53cf-ba24-e30a9d7def19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465394} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e938ae3-f27b-5e0d-93f6-fd7f5fbab6cf" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f9e2552-d78f-5856-897c-1066c7c11370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465395} {:answer/id #uuid "8e4fa949-854b-5ee7-8b85-75ab00ce9a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e4fa949-854b-5ee7-8b85-75ab00ce9a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465396} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ca3abf8-142e-5260-aec2-6a593434d8f3" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=4-z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466541} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2305890-a995-5d60-b9bd-dda89a17580d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465397} {:answer/id #uuid "85d5eb5f-70d4-55e0-9577-81a9d91ad5e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2305890-a995-5d60-b9bd-dda89a17580d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465397} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0610e88-6eb9-5b63-8129-a7376026d04c" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,z)=4-z$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466542}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8d0077c3-5809-5281-a04f-def492b7900c" :question/math-academy-id "q-161248" :question/problem "![](images/40/40091bf7a66577a4a3f3b8cdf3b5da34cbe0e0198fdc5731c6d3dae8cb727418.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=1$, $z=0$, $z=3$, $y=0,$ and $y=4-z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {f}_{2}(x,z)}\n$$\n\nas a type III region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c3333ded3e00e7d7408f0dbd37807f1adec0301691cc6311871bfea6d7b9fa15.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=4-z$” is true, while statement “${f}_{1}(x,z)=4-z$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=4$” is false. We have\n\n- the *left* surface $y={f}_{1}(x,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *right* surface $y={f}_{2}(x,z)=4-z.$\n\n![](images/b1/b1046e312a3783dfc3253646f8a71ae226a173ac882a6305850bdd81aed9dd7e.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; “${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=4-z$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278447 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133820 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dea8612-414c-5394-869d-1e404b048156" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type III Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175 :topic/id #uuid "85bac388-4397-5418-87a6-a1048f67cdda" :topic/math-academy-id 2130 :topic/title "Type I, II, and III Regions in Three-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87947aba-3ee6-5f0b-b3c6-cd6a066bd244" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465399} {:answer/id #uuid "97174b7f-38ab-52ee-b9d8-8cb8b66d0e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97174b7f-38ab-52ee-b9d8-8cb8b66d0e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465400} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5ae30f-59ec-58d7-a15c-4249798540d9" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1ea4a1-1147-5bfc-8507-1bf0d77960ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465401} {:answer/id #uuid "f84ca98d-56b9-5e97-bfb2-dff3175e39ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c1ea4a1-1147-5bfc-8507-1bf0d77960ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465401} :answer-field/id #uuid "73340b15-0013-5823-988c-a3ba50461d3c" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,z)=z-\\frac{x}{3}$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466544} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eae65db7-54ff-596a-b1e0-2327b0ecaba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465403} {:answer/id #uuid "23d0f29c-f34b-599c-8760-32746cd6d595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23d0f29c-f34b-599c-8760-32746cd6d595" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465404} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb2eb83-9dd5-5fd0-a343-cff27dd76ab1" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9bbc7b8c-0af0-5315-ba58-db2c9cd43206" :question/math-academy-id "q-161250" :question/problem "![](images/d4/d447e5a00aa324d83a3f513db11ff677fd2db2c7b1b33d8bc2bcfa73b4a08f3f.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $x=0$, $x=3$, $z=0$, $z=2$, $y=0,$ and $y=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(x,z)\\le y\\le {f}_{2}(x,z)}\n$$\n\nas a type III region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type III region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c3333ded3e00e7d7408f0dbd37807f1adec0301691cc6311871bfea6d7b9fa15.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $xz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(x,z)=z-\\frac{x}{3}$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3$” is false, while statement “${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z$” is true. We have\n\n- the *left* surface $y={f}_{1}(x,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *right* surface $y={f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z.$\n\n![](images/88/88b5fde383f094436dd94adefa7912f1a194319739fdb0b8a6a9a74693362219.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; “${f}_{1}(x,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(x,z)=3+\\frac{x}{3}-z$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278496 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133819 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7dcc1bf5-5eea-5615-8b16-b8ced5de7984" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Type II Regions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048175 :topic/id #uuid "85bac388-4397-5418-87a6-a1048f67cdda" :topic/math-academy-id 2130 :topic/title "Type I, II, and III Regions in Three-Dimensional Space"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "057db65a-eecb-52c7-ac69-c8a69baf0264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465405} {:answer/id #uuid "4640f754-7b8a-5863-a4a7-4984c1ec21a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4640f754-7b8a-5863-a4a7-4984c1ec21a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465406} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca4918c6-67e4-5f19-84fb-a1e03896cf0d" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25c8e774-2be1-50a4-be88-195ee7a64ff9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465407} {:answer/id #uuid "450f49eb-7a8d-5ee5-80f1-0b4c034f20a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "450f49eb-7a8d-5ee5-80f1-0b4c034f20a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465408} :answer-field/id #uuid "bed649e4-9512-5df5-8690-508a27d9b3e5" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466547} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "906a29e2-7f19-5c43-bd9f-25622a39d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465409} {:answer/id #uuid "b1856245-617f-5aa9-b2a6-f6ea110eeb7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "906a29e2-7f19-5c43-bd9f-25622a39d650" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465409} :answer-field/id #uuid "c51647d3-edd0-55aa-b2d7-68154b9214d2" :answer-field/key "${f}_{1}(y,z)=4+y-2z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466548}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f1a985-1f99-5d8b-a66e-0643cac8da20" :question/math-academy-id "q-161361" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7799ca5801bf019fc5b884590575346a8f298f8e9c91056c13a60c4dd23742d.png)\n\nThe region $R$ is bounded by the planes $y=0$, $y=4$, $z=0$, $z=3$, $x=0,$ and $x=4-y+2z.$ Given its representation \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,{f}_{1}(y,z)\\le x\\le {f}_{2}(y,z)}\n$$\n\nas a type II region in three-dimensional space, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A typical three-dimensional type II region can be visualized schematically, as shown below.\n\n![](images/e4/e4c9cbbad2f13e9cc125ddbb89125ed2d734eee3f80737125961f4af1846a972.png)\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ is true. The projection $D$ of the solid onto the $yz$-plane gives the domain \n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z$” is true and statement “${f}_{1}(y,z)=4+y-2z$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4$” is false. We have\n\n- the *back* surface $x={f}_{1}(y,z)=0$, and\n\n- the *front* surface $x={f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z.$\n\n![](images/3b/3bf8e141067fb6f675933f52e465114d8909d951f6ac85fb09c8dda7efbc2f38.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}D=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(y,z)\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\\\\\,0\\le z\\le 3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; “${f}_{1}(y,z)=0$ and ${f}_{2}(y,z)=4-y+2z$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f462a13-e52b-5f50-bd9b-5e3e04a75ec4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465417} {:answer/id #uuid "7d035b1f-7fbf-59ff-b61e-ebb312eee7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d035b1f-7fbf-59ff-b61e-ebb312eee7bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465418} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4834f1a-3776-5597-bca0-28aea74896d7" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4acc30dd-b0dd-5587-9188-4cc8367a69bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465419} {:answer/id #uuid "28f06c85-e623-54b7-9f55-9afd7009566f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28f06c85-e623-54b7-9f55-9afd7009566f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465420} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac548899-74b4-5b42-b1ca-0d1482e4229f" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le 3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466553} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb0fe9bc-f78c-5c55-bbf7-fd65e2ea1195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465421} {:answer/id #uuid "c615d31d-cf76-5762-8eca-1a561a4f0997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465422}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb0fe9bc-f78c-5c55-bbf7-fd65e2ea1195" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465421} :answer-field/id #uuid "28fa83d6-4600-547a-a25c-706ebb06a453" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,-1<x<1,\\\\\\,0<y<2-{x}^{2}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8fb05970-59dc-5904-9b90-0c1d735b4269" :question/math-academy-id "q-161638" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are closed?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\\\\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le 3}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278577 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1723e615-d467-58f5-999a-7973741641a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465423} {:answer/id #uuid "f9abc517-42f5-5df9-8763-751fa53ba7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1723e615-d467-58f5-999a-7973741641a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465423} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e72de96-4a0e-5793-9030-00840e107b1a" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,-3<x<-1,\\\\\\,1<y<0.5x+3\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #ed