b/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c3f47e10-181c-587e-a0be-2b1e263782c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161646" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The third set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }-3<x<3,\\\\\\,0<y<|2x|\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }-1<x<1,\\\\\\,1<y<3-{x}^{2}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"} :activity/title "Open and Closed Sets" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481577} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481678}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :k