" :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)={sec}^{2}⁡x \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({sec}^{2}⁡x)=2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,{sec}^{2}⁡x,2{sec}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x,…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is also infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)=-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x \\\\ {g}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x)=-27\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nB={\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x,-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x,-27\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x,…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is finite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ {h}^{(4)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $C$ contains four elements:\n\n$$\nC={3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|C|=4,$ which is finite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ and $B$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287731 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198271 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26758016-ed47-562a-9338-85c71ffbeaa9" :knowledge-point/title "Sets Defined Using Derivatives" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049070 :topic/id #uuid "d79ee816-b7eb-5805-856a-502f9a6adaa4" :topic/math-academy-id 4386 :topic/title "Infinite Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e96d9ecf-7714-57a9-822a-673f4c37e00b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465731} {:answer/id #uuid "d06c5adc-b6e6-5661-aa46-fe0af05aca05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d06c5adc-b6e6-5661-aa46-fe0af05aca05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465732} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d1f3fcf-a637-52be-a4cc-f4d0d0495ce9" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}A=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}{f}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(\\frac{1}{x})\\,:\\\\\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b58cb3-b8af-5ab4-a0b2-cd7710728247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465733} {:answer/id #uuid "87fba519-d6d9-503f-9d6d-bb77aaa0872a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b58cb3-b8af-5ab4-a0b2-cd7710728247" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465733} :answer-field/id #uuid "69a01e8f-100d-5baa-929b-6c8ad68c2833" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}B=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}{g}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}({x}^{3})\\,:\\\\\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c4d0d40-f6f1-57b6-851c-5449892b4591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465735} {:answer/id #uuid "e198b1e1-2401-5091-8cd1-9ee577cd7313" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465736}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c4d0d40-f6f1-57b6-851c-5449892b4591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465735} :answer-field/id #uuid "57b3697b-3114-5d98-939c-b7a32b8a561a" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}C=\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}{h}^{(n)}(x)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}(4x)\\,:\\\\\\,n\\in {N}_{0}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466711}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c54f5b27-abdd-5f0e-891e-7fb28f946241" :question/math-academy-id "q-181702" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements.\n\n- The set $A$ is infinite. Listing the first few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{(0)}(x) & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {f}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{x})=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {f}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})=\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}} \\\\ {f}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}})=-\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}} \\\\ ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we can write our set as follows:\n\n$$\nA={\\frac{1}{x},-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\frac{2}{{x}^{3}},-\\frac{6}{{x}^{4}},…}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $A$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $B$ is finite. Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{(0)}(x) & ={x}^{3} \\\\ {g}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})=3{x}^{2} \\\\ {g}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{2})=6x \\\\ {g}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6x)=6 \\\\ {g}^{(4)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6)=0 \\\\ {g}^{(5)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(0)=0 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, for $n>4,$ we have ${g}^{(n)}(x)=0.$ Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\nB={{x}^{3},3{x}^{2},6x,6,0}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|B|=5,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $C$ is also finite. Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{h}^{(0)}(x) & =4x \\\\ {h}^{(1)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x)=4 \\\\ {h}^{(2)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4)=0 \\\\ {h}^{(3)}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(0)=0 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, for $n>2,$ we have ${h}^{(n)}(x)=0.$ Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\nC={4x,4,0}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|C|=3,$ which is finite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287770 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a15d8068-a297-5b27-9571-7349edb98145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465761} {:answer/id #uuid "50699285-bf28-54d7-83ab-33d95b70f1dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50699285-bf28-54d7-83ab-33d95b70f1dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465762} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6e4a31d-6892-5f31-9c96-e11ca818307e" :answer-field/key "$(a,a,1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "857215ce-87c7-5d52-b667-daa2294c53fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465763} {:answer/id #uuid "d620ca5c-7969-5245-beb2-5c9f3507de3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d620ca5c-7969-5245-beb2-5c9f3507de3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465764} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed6bc72c-bbdd-5c3c-817f-ec5f93dbd78d" :answer-field/key "$(b,a,2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c10f6fae-2c1c-5519-902a-f8a1bbc36128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465765} {:answer/id #uuid "fd632de3-82a9-5dc9-9c61-6bd9d87107fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c10f6fae-2c1c-5519-902a-f8a1bbc36128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465765} :answer-field/id #uuid "8212bee8-04d9-5d5d-ad9b-4facf1dc8f94" :answer-field/key "$((a,b),2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466726}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e5ba42f9-2582-56fd-9cc1-974b79efc1dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-181941" :question/problem "If $A=\\{a,b\\}$ and $B=\\{1,2\\},$ which of the following elements belong to $A\\times A\\times B?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B\\times C$ consists of all ordered triples whose first coordinate belongs to $A,$ second coordinate belongs to $B,$ and the third coordinate belongs to $C.$\n\nIn this case, $A\\times A\\times B$ consists of every combination of $\\{a,b\\}$ with $\\{a,b\\}$ and $\\{1,2\\},$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\times A\\times B=\\{ & (a,a,1),(a,a,2),(a,b,1),(a,b,2), \\\\  & (b,a,1),(b,a,2),(b,b,1),(b,b,2)\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n|A\\times A\\times B|=|A|\\cdot |A|\\cdot |B|=2\\cdot 2\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, we see that both $(a,a,1)$ and $(b,a,2)$ are in $A\\times A\\times B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(a,a,1)$; $(b,a,2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054636 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fca5176-1359-5ad8-b012-592ffa9b20b5" :knowledge-point/title "Cartesian Products With Three Sets" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050432 :topic/id #uuid "48930849-af42-52a8-8e89-28eb54e1d4a5" :topic/math-academy-id 49 :topic/title "The Cartesian Product"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a46bf5c6-d6fe-5e42-af86-ce7600ded59e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465767} {:answer/id #uuid "e32e199d-4753-5a7e-9c53-1be55160b642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a46bf5c6-d6fe-5e42-af86-ce7600ded59e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465767} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca389aa0-4d8b-5422-93e9-74e7c9056c63" :answer-field/key "$(9,9,y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466727} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61f781e7-9f4f-5947-9dea-30b3c6a60411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465769} {:answer/id #uuid "92da6a17-19ff-5528-aee1-eb979f83f3c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61f781e7-9f4f-5947-9dea-30b3c6a60411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465769} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ed0697c-624f-503f-bf92-0cc49285c227" :answer-field/key "$(8,x,y)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466728} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5db7bb44-599d-522c-8a9c-70f7761b0faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218646577