f its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,0).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\\\\\,0<{y}^{2}\\le 2\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\\\\\,0\\le x<1,\\\\\\,{y}^{2}<4\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/title "Quiz 2" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186538217} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539080}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6044dc-d4a7-5662-a825-3c13e49d198a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets That are Neither Open Nor Closed" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/id #uuid "9f807cd5-8888-510e-98d9-a7920b0d7b50" :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11c4606f-5c57-58fd-9b55-f0f565399e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467890} {:answer/id #uuid "839ad9eb-979f-5d6a-9652-cf932de67c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11c4606f-5c57-58fd-9b55-f0f565399e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467890} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0dbd3ff-e733-5ef8-8e2a-4b6a3ed482cc" :answer-field/key "${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468666} {:answer-fie