ght\\}\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be4d8952-950b-5fb0-a574-0337f64e1d84" :question/math-academy-id "q-161648" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }0<x<3,\\\\\\,0<y<6-2x\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$; $\\begin{gathered}\\left\\{\\begin{gathered}(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\\\\\text{ }1<x<4,\\\\\\,x<y<{x}^{2}\\end{gathered}\\right\\}\\end{gathered}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380664 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172085 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "019e5a17-1aab-565b-8881-447c86a9a7ec" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Two-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1447082-f4e8-5788-a80e-d8c2f8b82522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437630} {:answer/id #uuid "747beaa6-cbb1-5ab8-b6f0-aac6db2ca380" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1447082-f4e8-5788-a80e-d8c2f8b82522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437630} :answer-field/id #uuid "89920c46-71c7-5175-8718-e990046088f6" :answer-field/key "$M(x,y)$ $=⟨y-{x}^{2},3x+{y}^{2},\\frac{1}{x+y}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5963b314-2add-567a-b457-6f81885a3dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437632} {:answer/id #uuid "0a97ce34-6fad-5a23-a913-7a8c54c9939c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a97ce34-6fad-5a23-a913-7a8c54c9939c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437633} :answer-field/id #uuid "121c69dd-36e1-570a-bd6d-c832cafb4cd4" :answer-field/key "$N(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1,1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2852e063-18c2-5c27-805a-899fefe85cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437634} {:answer/id #uuid "2d47eb09-37b1-5b48-8d81-6237d57c3ab0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2852e063-18c2-5c27-805a-899fefe85cd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437634} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6caeebf-8412-599a-8bb3-625ed3e2bddb" :answer-field/key "$P(t)=⟨{t}^{3},\\sqrt{1-t}\\,⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "502cb71c-02d6-5e14-a31b-2cee28a0a5ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-122656" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{2}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{2}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y)$ in $S$ to a vector $F(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $M(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  ${R}^{2}$ to vectors in ${R}^{3}$ (not in ${R}^{2}$).\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It maps every point $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}$ to a vector in ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The function $P(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{2}.$ It assigns points in  $R$ \n(not ${R}^{2}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $N(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1,1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380692 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa463bcd-c692-5b2e-81fb-6edd382301d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437654} {:answer/id #uuid "0f0c189c-4360-5311-8733-688846ac83f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa463bcd-c692-5b2e-81fb-6edd382301d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437654} :answer-field/id #uuid "eec2a251-816b-560e-984e-218cc993a24b" :answer-field/key "$P(x,y)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,i+(x+y)^{2}\\,j$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438856} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e7e53ee-c545-556b-8c01-71673e0ac9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437656} {:answer/id #uuid "133f3ccd-0846-5c2f-8e29-aac997ab0c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437657}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "133f3ccd-0846-5c2f-8e29-aac997ab0c45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437657} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e2fd0e0-3c93-53a1-8f8a-f97251928fc1" :answer-field/key "$Q(x,y,z)$ $=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i$ $-\\frac{x}{y}\\,j$ $+\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22acadb3-7ca8-5abe-ad3c-4d0f8a82b17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437658} {:answer/id #uuid "bafa02fd-27b6-50a3-b21c-bc14c4e05eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437659}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22acadb3-7ca8-5abe-ad3c-4d0f8a82b17b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437658} :answer-field/id #uuid "a898dd6a-8e9a-579f-bcba-72e40817966d" :answer-field/key "$R(t)=\\frac{1}{t+1}\\,i-(3t-1)\\,j+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b17979a9-57b7-5c2d-8065-c277267e307e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122686" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $P(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $Q(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,z\\ne -1,\\,y\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $R(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $Q(x,y,z)$ $=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,i$ $-\\frac{x}{y}\\,j$ $+\\frac{1}{z+1}\\,k$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186380699 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172087 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb34fdb0-198e-507d-a944-9be782b4cfeb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields on Three-Dimensions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050412 :topic/id #uuid "46db30fb-cff1-5fef-85ad-641fbb5c68f2" :topic/math-academy-id 3343 :topic/title "Vector Fields"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91acbdcb-0819-512d-8f3a-8f5b18843d8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437678} {:answer/id #uuid "c042a6b6-5fe6-5670-9ac7-c7152c415d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c042a6b6-5fe6-5670-9ac7-c7152c415d96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437679} :answer-field/id #uuid "78ff1394-a615-59ad-bb26-46d4946b7591" :answer-field/key "$M(x,y,z)$ $=⟨z-{x}^{2},3x+{z}^{2},\\frac{1}{x+y}⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77a73f89-d276-53da-ba0d-e39074166f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437680} {:answer/id #uuid "83b30725-25b3-5535-9453-a881c12cb3ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77a73f89-d276-53da-ba0d-e39074166f8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437680} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a11b4f3-6da8-5671-9b65-64280b7f35aa" :answer-field/key "$N(x,y)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡y+1,1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438869} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c27113d-a2f3-54dd-a0fe-40e814f8066c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437682} {:answer/id #uuid "88e9a9b2-4f69-57eb-9973-f4cc63d15d74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c27113d-a2f3-54dd-a0fe-40e814f8066c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437682} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6f83e16-f061-5b3d-ae8a-955bb9e63305" :answer-field/key "$P(t)=⟨{t}^{3},\\sqrt{1-t}\\,⟩$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "438dc864-2346-5ec7-8b61-791bfb4d3c82" :question/math-academy-id "q-122695" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $M(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,x+y\\ne 0}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $N(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $P(t)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in $R$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $M(x,y,z)$ $=⟨z-{x}^{2},3x+{z}^{2},\\frac{1}{x+y}⟩$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8f012d0-444a-5035-8a72-a053de312d63" :knowledge-point/title "Changing the Order of Integration" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050207 :topic/id #uuid "36521b0a-e13c-5296-b2d4-078f2470ad6d" :topic/math-academy-id 1992 :topic/title "Double Integrals Over Rectangular Domains"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c1ebce9-eb86-5d86-ac05-3d046c19d154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471507} {:answer/id #uuid "191266bf-17fa-5b3f-a69d-006602f0b1f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c1ebce9-eb86-5d86-ac05-3d046c19d154" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471507} :answer-field/id #uuid "51a227da-90c2-52f9-9077-b27b96efcf2d" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472259} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee27b98a-d403-540e-b4d1-58599c0791ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471509} {:answer/id #uuid "28c28979-9f71-531a-95a5-9727b10ce997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28c28979-9f71-531a-95a5-9727b10ce997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471510} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3d0d5f5-af4c-574f-bc3d-7168cd1ab3e6" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472260} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfbf44d-eb98-55d5-8c14-3e22b731f235" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471511} {:answer/id #uuid "98822c58-2bb2-5161-be03-5dc25f69be74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98822c58-2bb2-5161-be03-5dc25f69be74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471512} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e78bf6a-ca6f-5737-8263-4c7e4e4b8a4d" :answer-field/key "${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472261}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d63a269e-ef04-5d49-b4b0-245cf68e9dfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-72167" :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $-2$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-1$ to $-1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-2}^{2}[{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$; ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A$ $={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383466 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050835 :topic/id #uuid "6a5936fb-0bab-5b84-a342-e13ec8019ebc" :topic/math-academy-id 3048 :topic/title "Independence of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b7c73a6-2af0-5b92-b6f9-3d93e71ac279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453410} {:answer/id #uuid "cd588ae9-2b60-5171-90a5-e75b1b1f4e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd588ae9-2b60-5171-90a5-e75b1b1f4e4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453411} :answer-field/id #uuid "e212ea0e-0893-522d-b146-c4a56808a680" :answer-field/key "$P(X=1,Y=2)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454455} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3e69a34-93a1-5a43-834c-4e189751c4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453412} {:answer/id #uuid "2d4c23a1-a357-5eb9-9f99-65ce1db5f659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d4c23a1-a357-5eb9-9f99-65ce1db5f659" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453413} :answer-field/id #uuid "79de55e8-6943-548b-a367-c214c3149889" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454456} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f17d2094-f158-54e5-846d-74fedf6ed19e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453414} {:answer/id #uuid "68e664fb-4f6e-51e7-b3d4-8922d50069a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453415}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68e664fb-4f6e-51e7-b3d4-8922d50069a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453415} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ed06e01-142b-5c2b-b22f-d3c32e2dbb48" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47bb5e3d-7de9-53ad-b629-7512a9b347ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-143328" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.15$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ | $0.75$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.4$ | $0.6$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=1,Y=2)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=1,Y=2)=f(1,2)=0.15.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.25\\cdot 0.6=0.15.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true. Checking all other possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =0.1=0.25\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(2,1) & =0.3=0.75\\cdot 0.4={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & ✓ \\\\ f(2,2) & =0.45=0.75\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2) & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is true. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is true, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ must be independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=1,Y=2)$ $=P(X=1)\\cdot P(Y=2)$; “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$”; “$X$ and $Y$ are independent”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162153 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "196e7d31-5af8-5c82-b2bd-0cf1ed7415e2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Random Variables are Independent Given the Joint PMF Only" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050835 :topic/id #uuid "6a5936fb-0bab-5b84-a342-e13ec8019ebc" :topic/math-academy-id 3048 :topic/title "Independence of Discrete Random Variables"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98db4bdf-35c0-572f-a8d0-dd5af5d2d797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471045} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5b1cde-3a17-5c26-ae0b-684c07d6c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e5b1cde-3a17-5c26-ae0b-684c07d6c465" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471046} :answer-field/id #uuid "28b9829d-7120-5b5c-92bd-c1ef0c0e2fa6" :answer-field/key "$P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472028} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9127507d-cd00-5560-bb89-a83a30f508fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471047} {:answer/id #uuid "ba4074bd-8e93-5f12-a606-f60e237bc602" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9127507d-cd00-5560-bb89-a83a30f508fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471047} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bbaf59b-eeb3-51ce-8a01-5dc52517e99d" :answer-field/key "$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472029} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf59bd71-a0bd-5b9f-a650-5a3684e0a341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471049} {:answer/id #uuid "ee3117e1-426e-540f-a519-e302a751ae0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf59bd71-a0bd-5b9f-a650-5a3684e0a341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471049} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d335f5-b08f-5856-be51-b11cb49c2f5f" :answer-field/key "$X$ and $Y$ are independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5449cbef-825d-5bac-be24-822940400b4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-143335" :question/problem "The joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ |\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nComputing the marginal probability mass functions for  $X$ and $Y,$ we obtain the following:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ | $0.5$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.2$ | $0.1$ | $0.3$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $0.6$ | $0.4$ | $1$ |\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement $P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=2,Y=2)=f(2,2)=0.2.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)={f}_{X}(2)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(2)=0.5\\cdot 0.4=0.2.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false. Taking $x=1$ and $y=1,$ we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,1) & =0.1\\ne 0.2\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(1)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement “$X$ and $Y$ are independent” is false. Since statement “$P(X=x,Y=y)$ $=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$” is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $P(X=2,Y=2)$ $=P(X=2)\\cdot P(Y=2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3868de94-f40b-55e1-bdb2-a7150e6b6c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471311} {:answer/id #uuid "631e930d-695f-5af5-aab9-dd585c953e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "631e930d-695f-5af5-aab9-dd585c953e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471312} :answer-field/id #uuid "66365a99-0b60-58bb-94f2-ccec01ad35dc" :answer-field/key "$R⊆R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472161} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b15f1878-c363-590e-a18b-cef0bf952481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471313} {:answer/id #uuid "e1261589-bf12-56e1-ba17-0ecce5d607fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b15f1878-c363-590e-a18b-cef0bf952481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471313} :answer-field/id #uuid "2578266a-3ab5-5ff5-8e6f-8c792ea992ef" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472162} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed69226c-011b-5b2e-b15f-abdaa112a0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471315} {:answer/id #uuid "25d82bff-bad4-53b1-a8f4-aac1a9c3dd94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed69226c-011b-5b2e-b15f-abdaa112a0e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471315} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7610904-dd5b-5286-aa99-f44196a2d25e" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{2}\\in Z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "878c8bf5-19ec-5026-9004-ee961047a572" :question/math-academy-id "q-215831" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $\\sqrt{3}\\in R$, then $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}}.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is trivial?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overbrace{Q}^{\\text{Always true}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Statement $R⊆R$ is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate ${x}^{2}=0$, defined for $x\\in R,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement $\\frac{1}{2}\\in Z$ is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $R⊆R$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384691 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf9e4aa9-8e45-51b3-b3b8-086dc158a25a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471317} {:answer/id #uuid "1dec0be7-4806-59e3-98b0-14968d4a61d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf9e4aa9-8e45-51b3-b3b8-086dc158a25a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471317} :answer-field/id #uuid "848d2e24-735f-5301-9b27-a19033fd2df7" :answer-field/key "$n$ is even" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472164} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c955bf8-730b-5d76-a57b-8e87b63787ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471