true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overbrace{Q}^{\\text{Always true}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Predicate “$n$ is even”, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $1-{n}^{2}<2$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate $1<n<2$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $1-{n}^{2}<2$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384698 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4fb3905-55df-5307-b742-1b5ee71becee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471323} {:answer/id #uuid "687a1f83-58ae-59c6-980d-748e61017f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "687a1f83-58ae-59c6-980d-748e61017f57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471324} :answer-field/id #uuid "e83dfcb0-1487-55a7-8777-e4c33fed1869" :answer-field/key "$1-|x|\\in Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472167} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94dcd398-9bb3-5c23-96f9-4f66db4bc936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471325} {:answer/id #uuid "1f3f307c-9cc7-5489-9c08-b3829f93e87c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94dcd398-9bb3-5c23-96f9-4f66db4bc936" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471325} :answer-field/id #uuid "e360c1f4-9aa4-5f8d-995e-c5dae8c3dccf" :answer-field/key "${2}^{-1}<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472168} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a60a4bc-ff1b-5642-b8ce-d94e871ade4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471327} {:answer/id #uuid "91c7bc32-ec83-550e-b184-be712e2fd199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a60a4bc-ff1b-5642-b8ce-d94e871ade4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471327} :answer-field/id #uuid "07987a83-6f45-5147-a121-27bc2d71e9c2" :answer-field/key "$x>1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f7628b9b-2926-5b1b-a6ec-eba49d9a9a32" :question/math-academy-id "q-216030" :question/problem "Let $x\\in Q.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If ${x}^{-1}<1,$ then $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}}.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is trivial?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overbrace{Q}^{\\text{Always true}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Predicate $1-|x|\\in Q$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement ${2}^{-1}<0$ is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $x>1$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $1-|x|\\in Q$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384705 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45f828cb-c8b1-5da4-9711-15ace712dffa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Vacuous Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34a0c713-82a0-5e54-9195-49999007aaeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471329} {:answer/id #uuid "3bae32ae-2fcf-5066-b6d8-5261a2ca782c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34a0c713-82a0-5e54-9195-49999007aaeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471329} :answer-field/id #uuid "717c53c5-7f91-58f1-9901-986694b231d1" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{x}{5}\\in Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d835ee88-916c-51b8-930a-3f05b769c7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471331} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca904fc-ca69-54bd-aa4a-aec576a4d75b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d835ee88-916c-51b8-930a-3f05b769c7c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471331} :answer-field/id #uuid "f593a20c-89bf-5395-9a4e-db70094a586b" :answer-field/key "$x>0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a53a23a-e29e-5a76-8fc5-012d2015edb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471333} {:answer/id #uuid "66e0a6b4-fe1e-57e5-8831-32ec67ae7066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66e0a6b4-fe1e-57e5-8831-32ec67ae7066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471334} :answer-field/id #uuid "9104dafe-72f4-5668-810d-9347cbc93cc9" :answer-field/key "$|x|<-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "576618c9-5633-5684-823b-e6a81214839e" :question/math-academy-id "q-216041" :question/problem "Let $x\\in Q.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}},$ then $\\sqrt{x}\\in C.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is vacuous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *vacuous proof* if the antecedent is always false: \n\n$$\n\\overbrace{P}^{\\text{Always false}}⇒\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our antecedents in turn.\n\n- Predicate $\\frac{x}{5}\\in Q$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $x>0$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $|x|<-1$, defined for $x\\in Q,$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $|x|<-1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45f828cb-c8b1-5da4-9711-15ace712dffa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Vacuous Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b39e76-bc8c-52a1-9ab4-8b53fc905cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471335} {:answer/id #uuid "cff96380-a1c0-587a-987e-3f2acfcaf2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30b39e76-bc8c-52a1-9ab4-8b53fc905cc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471335} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e2c93d8-0870-5cf3-b105-7f99a6eb460c" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{5}\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97bca418-db97-5bac-b2db-02fcefe49965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471337} {:answer/id #uuid "29f98fe9-52bd-59fd-8edc-d7d75dee4b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29f98fe9-52bd-59fd-8edc-d7d75dee4b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471338} :answer-field/id #uuid "4096e8f7-5304-599d-ad95-c167b5f3267f" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{2}\\in Z$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d431875-8e83-5eba-909d-822a0ec932c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471339} {:answer/id #uuid "772955b8-21e1-5817-8746-49e813d39f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d431875-8e83-5eba-909d-822a0ec932c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471339} :answer-field/id #uuid "a890f1e2-6f72-5c8e-a3de-abe895d3b730" :answer-field/key "${x}^{5}>1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a08b61dd-f4dd-592d-9272-a1584fed8eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-216045" :question/problem "Let $x\\in R.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}},$ then ${x}^{2}+2x<-1.$ \n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is vacuous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *vacuous proof* if the antecedent is always false: \n\n$$\n\\overbrace{P}^{\\text{Always false}}⇒\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our antecedents in turn.\n\n- Statement $\\sqrt{5}\\in R$ is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement $\\sqrt{2}\\in Z$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\n- Predicate ${x}^{5}>1$, defined for $x\\in R,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\sqrt{2}\\in Z$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45f828cb-c8b1-5da4-9711-15ace712dffa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Vacuous Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7fc458-0426-5cb1-b0f0-1e31fe748ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471341} {:answer/id #uuid "47405ffc-cfec-5943-9bf9-2b89f47af34f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c7fc458-0426-5cb1-b0f0-1e31fe748ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471341} :answer-field/id #uuid "552f79a8-e7b3-522e-8b3d-7198b74bc8d0" :answer-field/key "$n+1>n$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472176} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9bd9c434-2c4b-562c-839d-16f535749a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471343} {:answer/id #uuid "70dacb19-1349-50ce-91a6-ff0482a093eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bd9c434-2c4b-562c-839d-16f535749a96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471343} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c146e66-86e6-5c00-a6d7-c99086687a70" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{n}\\in Q$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3651db8-a40c-5179-a9d5-6b9b5175df38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471345} {:answer/id #uuid "244fec6a-6e2d-5599-a615-d61746598608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471346}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "244fec6a-6e2d-5599-a615-d61746598608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471346} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d30d3dd-a0e3-5689-8bf5-241b949d0faa" :answer-field/key "$0<n<1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abf1ead3-58c2-53df-80ac-6b0af0110700" :question/math-academy-id "q-216046" :question/problem "Let $n\\in Z.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}},$ then ${n}^{2}<0.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is vacuous?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *vacuous proof* if the antecedent is always false: \n\n$$\n\\overbrace{P}^{\\text{Always false}}⇒\\,Q\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the consequent is true or false. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our antecedents in turn.\n\n- Predicate $n+1>n$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always true. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $\\sqrt{n}\\in Q$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is *not* always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate $0<n<1$, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is always false. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $0<n<1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186384726 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157233 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "45f828cb-c8b1-5da4-9711-15ace712dffa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Vacuous Statement" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fecc96dc-05fb-5de3-b963-2e113cb27686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471347} {:answer/id #uuid "988fc342-37b6-508a-a091-ab91d627f455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fecc96dc-05fb-5de3-b963-2e113cb27686" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471347} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d82d74d-0ab4-5e70-91b9-bd0c7a9dfd4e" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{5}\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472179} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56ea38e7-97ac-50c0-bc84-297846484eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471349} {:answer/id #uuid "1ec15986-de28-5b61-9ef3-660fdfc28027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ec15986-de28-5b61-9ef3-660fdfc28027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471350} :answer-field/id #uuid "83156a