orrect answer is ${cos}^{2}⁡x>1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385666 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157232 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb4d348b-1703-51a1-be05-2e66295cacaa" :knowledge-point/title "Completing Trivial Statements" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049554 :topic/id #uuid "fed99c84-950a-5788-8cb4-d3c785359494" :topic/math-academy-id 2815 :topic/title "Trivial and Vacuous Proofs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d651d58c-8505-5b88-9051-45a55fccbbca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471567} {:answer/id #uuid "2084d778-f394-5120-a035-085334534098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471568}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2084d778-f394-5120-a035-085334534098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471568} :answer-field/id #uuid "104907a6-cdd1-5226-80af-9238e48719dd" :answer-field/key "$3$ is odd" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472289} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4b7c76e-4f1a-5a35-aaa7-113b98824a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471569} {:answer/id #uuid "c90a8158-3fa5-5544-8d1c-0590cb740f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4b7c76e-4f1a-5a35-aaa7-113b98824a0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471569} :answer-field/id #uuid "589fa4b5-e0cb-50a2-b3be-bd03ef21925e" :answer-field/key "$4$ is odd" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472290} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f04a6ac-0317-5ec8-b5dd-387f9a8446f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471571} {:answer/id #uuid "83d71d17-2958-5621-b3bc-0a068a57dce6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f04a6ac-0317-5ec8-b5dd-387f9a8446f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471571} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8267449-e179-58cb-88c0-3d4f6726b361" :answer-field/key "$n$ is odd" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6066c3ca-d4e8-51fc-956b-cd9926b46fbc" :question/math-academy-id "q-80083" :question/problem "Let $n\\in Z.$ Consider the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ If $2$ is even, then $\\underline{\\hspace{3em}}.$\n\nWhich of the following could be placed into the blank space above to create a statement whose proof is trivial?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that an implication has a *trivial proof* if the consequent is always true:\n\n$$\nP\\,⇒\\overbrace{Q}^{\\text{Always true}}\n$$\n\nIt does not matter whether the antecedent is true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our consequents in turn.\n\n- Statement “$3$ is odd” is always true. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement “$4$ is odd” is always false. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Predicate “$n$ is odd”, defined for $n\\in Z,$ is *not* always true. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$3$ is odd” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394057 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0b15f59e-ef74-5fa2-9af9-448fdcbbbd3d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Possible Pairs of First-Order Partial Derivatives" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049696 :topic/id #uuid "0bfad6b0-12ee-58d9-8324-1f301647b82f" :topic/math-academy-id 1957 :topic/title "Equality of Mixed Partial Derivatives"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de855fe1-6aff-57db-86ff-8ce6879436d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471639} {:answer/id #uuid "90632757-8919-58b6-bfed-61661c939a63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90632757-8919-58b6-bfed-61661c939a63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471640} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb9da46b-c58e-5af7-8e32-99a8a9fce27a" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)=x+3y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2{e}^{y}+3x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b1dca6b-130f-5024-a3e9-4606f7a93f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471641} {:answer/id #uuid "489d2221-0d68-5c98-9dcc-5350002296c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1dca6b-130f-5024-a3e9-4606f7a93f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471641} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4cdfb6d-5811-5893-91cb-282a189e3dd2" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)={x}^{2}+{e}^{x}+y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2x+{y}^{2}+{e}^{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472326} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f426f513-c9ed-5df4-a21b-26cc46b017a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471643} {:answer/id #uuid "ef52d1b0-46f6-5a4f-9dde-6750a336e7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f426f513-c9ed-5df4-a21b-26cc46b017a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471643} :answer-field/id #uuid "73f083bf-96db-5c32-aea8-1d7b3455b6ab" :answer-field/key "${f}_{x}(x,y)$ $=2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ $+xy$ $+5$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)={sin}^{2}⁡x+xy-2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472327}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ea0748a-6bf5-5641-b2b0-ad6357ffcd5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80757" :question/problem "Suppose that the function $f(x,y)$ and all of its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U.$ Which of the following pairs could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since the function and its first and second-order partial derivatives are continuous on an open set $U,$ the mixed partial derivatives must be equal, that is, ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y).$ Let's check if this condition is true for each of our pairs of first-order partial derivatives.\n\n- For the first pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+3y)=3 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{e}^{y}+3x)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)={f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the first pair could represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the second pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+{e}^{x}+y)=1 \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+{y}^{2}+{e}^{y})=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$, the second pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\n- For the third pair, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{xy}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+xy+5)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+x \\\\ {f}_{yx}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({sin}^{2}⁡x+xy-2)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs ${f}_{xy}(x,y)\\ne {f}_{yx}(x,y)$,  the third pair cannot represent the first-order partial derivatives of $f(x,y).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is '“${f}_{x}(x,y)=x+3y$ and ${f}_{y}(x,y)=2{e}^{y}+3x$” only'."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186078493 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62736299-f6d6-503f-a5d1-e1091e8b0429" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Convergent Geometric Series" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050868 :topic/id #uuid "6cc04ddb-ad7b-51e8-8f9d-c71c72f8e9d4" :topic/math-academy-id 684 :topic/title "Convergence of Geometric Series"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4259c2a-e037-547f-ba6f-c09ebc5c66e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470937} {:answer/id #uuid "93b837fb-dba3-5553-903e-a4ce54621dfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470938}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4259c2a-e037-547f-ba6f-c09ebc5c66e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470937} :answer-field/id #uuid "b837ace8-23d9-5324-878d-853d536782fd" :answer-field/key "$-1+1-1+1-⋯$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471974} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9227e56-d78e-5113-b51b-4b43a7893634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470939} {:answer/id #uuid "76dafe01-8b75-51aa-95ee-e47c3e5b805d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470940}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76dafe01-8b75-51aa-95ee-e47c3e5b805d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470940} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dcaf81f-0ef1-5a8a-bef8-bc4b434fc677" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{4}{3}-1+\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{9}{16}+⋯$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471975} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c50ac6cc-b478-5878-9ce1-12b1bc9ba137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470941} {:answer/id #uuid "e8414a63-aa61-5abf-b05d-7a72e20164ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c50ac6cc-b478-5878-9ce1-12b1bc9ba137" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470941} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e23d4f5-0d62-58e8-b892-40daa1d8e271" :answer-field/key "$\\begin{gathered}0.1+0.11+0.121+0.133\\,1+⋯\\end{gathered}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186471976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "55c1789a-3f1b-5ebc-a34c-eaab270f436c" :question/math-academy-id "q-124912" :question/problem "Which of the following geometric series converge?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each series in turn.\n\n- For the geometric series $-1+1-1+1-⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{1}{-1} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $\\frac{4}{3}-1+\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{9}{16}+⋯$ the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{(-1)}{(\\frac{4}{3})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is convergent because $|r|<1.$\n\n- For the geometric series $\\begin{gathered}0.1+0.11+0.121+0.133\\,1+⋯\\end{gathered}$  the common ratio is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=\\frac{{a}_{2}}{{a}_{1}} & =\\frac{0.11}{0.1} \\\\  & =1.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the series is divergent  because $|r|\\ge 1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only series $\\frac{4}{3}-1+\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{9}{16}+⋯$ converges."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152276 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Initial Value Problems" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050677 :topic/id #uuid "5e132315-9606-5b30-bee3-61f0209d40c4" :topic/math-academy-id 2548 :topic/title "Introduction to Second-Order Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f3327c5-5b2a-5b75-9864-25603f101b97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472670} {:answer/id #uuid "cd76ef06-44e2-5754-b673-0df8c217d82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472671}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd76ef06-44e2-5754-b673-0df8c217d82f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472671} :answer-field/id #uuid "44168093-c10a-5d0a-8140-ec50530f4e49" :answer-field/key "$5{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y$ $=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(0)$ $=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8777ff23-d174-5667-8e1f-e6c3e117ab9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472672} {:answer/id #uuid "2dc36741-bfd4-5924-8053-01816df989ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8777ff23-d174-5667-8e1f-e6c3e117ab9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472672} :answer-field/id #uuid "6718b63b-805d-5948-97da-74393d3fb5ba" :answer-field/key "${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-{e}^{x}{y}^{′}$ $=0,$ $\\,y(0)$ $=1,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(1)$ $=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473731} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71701165-79b0-527d-b2a4-9b177d828615" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472674} {:answer/id #uuid "9eee5dd1-afa1-5ed4-b8b2-4ac6dc7876a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9eee5dd1-afa1-5ed4-b8b2-4ac6dc7876a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472675} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fd34cea-273a-53f0-96bd-f7662dd63ffa" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{″}+{x}^{2}{y}^{′}$ $={e}^{x},$ $\\,y(1)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(1)$ $=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473732}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "30c6fcc7-4b73-56ac-a7b7-837e8d6bcc9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-130998" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$).\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=1$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152281 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a34d342c-e7fc-581b-b3d1-ed6a49f1a62f" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Boundary Value Problems" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049324 :topic/id #uuid "ebff858d-86f0-5d5d-b497-f8fb2d20cce6" :topic/math-academy-id 2742 :topic/title "Introduction to Boundary Value Problems"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b33f4ea-eb87-5a10-9db9-b7060a761d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473064} {:answer/id #uuid "69700ab0-c164-55f2-a3ee-f6417efe3d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473065}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b33f4ea-eb87-5a10-9db9-b7060a761d33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473064} :answer-field/id #uuid "84c54142-24d8-5e31-86ee-c1250b8bd6d1" :answer-field/key "$4{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\,y(0)=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473927} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6696cf6e-cfb2-5f0b-af4a-87a52e42df26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473066} {:answer/id #uuid "75536d10-6f3a-5468-a75f-4c616860138d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75536d10-6f3a-5468-a75f-4c616860138d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473067} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3dfc732-f8ca-5d4d-8efb-65f422851544" :answer-field/key "${y}^{″}+xy$ $={e}^{x},$ $\\,y(1)$ $=0,$ $\\,y(3)$ $=2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473928} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3095ce6-3605-5e05-9148-e2f97eb9e6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473068} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b40c26-33d9-54de-ba97-6856c59ae600" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3095ce6-3605-5e05-9148-e2f97eb9e6c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref